# GradeBoss golden rules (always apply)

Every feature, page, component, and change in this app MUST satisfy both rules
below. A change is not complete until both hold. See `AGENTS.md` for full detail.

## 1. Responsive & adaptive (desktop, macOS, Android, iOS)

- Write CSS mobile-first; add larger layouts with `min-width` media queries.
  Reuse the existing breakpoints: `600px` (tablet) and `900px` (desktop).
- Adapt navigation by form factor (bottom tab bar + top bar on phones,
  sidebar on desktop) as implemented in `client/src/App.tsx` and
  `client/src/styles.css`.
- Use fluid sizing (`clamp()`, `%`, `fr`, `minmax()`); avoid fixed pixel widths
  for viewport-spanning elements.
- Honor safe areas via the `--safe-*` variables (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`) and
  keep `viewport-fit=cover`. Prefer `100dvh` over `100vh`.
- Touch targets ~44px; form inputs `font-size: 16px` to avoid iOS zoom.
- Make wide content (tables) scroll instead of overflowing on small screens.

## 2. Installable & offline-capable (PWA)

- Maintain the PWA setup in `client/vite.config.ts` (`vite-plugin-pwa`):
  manifest, icons, service worker.
- Precache new static assets; add new offline-relevant API calls to the Workbox
  `runtimeCaching` rules (API GETs use `NetworkFirst`).
- Keep the app shell working offline and surface offline state to the user.
- Ensure `navigateFallback` covers any new routes so refresh works offline.

## Verify before finishing

Check phone (~390px), tablet (~768px), and desktop (~1280px) widths, and confirm
the built app registers a service worker and loads offline.
